<title>USA: Northrop, Hughes decline comment.</title>
<headline>Northrop, Hughes decline comment.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northrop Grumman Corp declined to comment on reports it raised its bid for Hughes Electronics Corp to around $10 billion.</p>
<p>&quot;As a matter of policy we don't comment on anything regarding mergers and aquisitions,&quot; spokesman Jim Hart told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Boston Globe reported Friday that Northrop and rival bidder Raytheon Co each raised their offers for the General Motors Corp unit to around $10 billion, and GM was to hold a board of directors meeting Friday to consider the bids.</p>
<p>A spokewoman for Hughes also declined to comment on the report.</p>
<p>Both companies added about $1 billion to their final bids submitted on Wednesday, persons close to the bidding told the newspaper.</p>
